==English==

==={{initialism}}===
'''GED'''

# {{US|education}} The GED® mark is a branded term and registered trademark owned by the American Council on Education for a battery of tests derived from the original coined phrase “tests of General Educational Development.” Upon passing the GED® tests, the student receives a high school equivalency diploma, a substitute for a high school diploma, for people who dropped out of high school or were [[homeschool]]ed.

